{
  "film": "026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star",
  "shots": "02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/rough_v04_pack/cuts_v04.json",
  "words": "02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/02_Voiceover/words.json",
  "sentences": [
    {
      "n": 1,
      "at": "0:00",
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 4.94,
      "text": "Look up on a clear night and the stars seem close, scattered just above the rooftops.",
      "row": "1",
      "source": "uhd_yb_paranal_01.mp4",
      "frame": "in-point",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/timelapse/uhd_yb_paranal_01.mp4",
      "also": [
        {
          "row": "1",
          "source": "iss073e0982261.jpg",
          "at": "0:03"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "n": 2,
      "at": "0:05",
      "start": 5.62,
      "end": 7.44,
      "text": "So how far away is the nearest one?",
      "row": "1",
      "source": "iss073e0982261.jpg",
      "frame": "still",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/nightsky/iss073e0982261.jpg",
      "also": []
    },
    {
      "n": 3,
      "at": "0:08",
      "start": 8.54,
      "end": 13.18,
      "text": "Light, the fastest thing there is, takes more than four years to cross the gap.",
      "row": "2",
      "source": "uhd_bt_paranal_01.mp4",
      "frame": "in-point",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/timelapse/uhd_bt_paranal_01.mp4",
      "also": []
    },
    {
      "n": 4,
      "at": "0:13",
      "start": 13.9,
      "end": 15.26,
      "text": "And here is the strange part.",
      "row": "3",
      "source": "uhd_bt_paranal_06.mp4",
      "frame": "in-point",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/timelapse/uhd_bt_paranal_06.mp4",
      "also": []
    },
    {
      "n": 5,
      "at": "0:15",
      "start": 15.88,
      "end": 19.34,
      "text": "You cannot see that star at all, not without a telescope.",
      "row": "3",
      "source": "potw1343a.jpg",
      "frame": "still",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/proxima/potw1343a.jpg",
      "also": [
        {
          "row": "3",
          "source": "uhd_bt_paranal_06.mp4",
          "at": "0:13"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "n": 6,
      "at": "0:20",
      "start": 20.88,
      "end": 32.7,
      "text": "In this film, I will show you which star it is, how anyone measured a distance that large, what that gap looks like if you shrink the whole thing down to fit on Earth, and how long it would take to get there.",
      "row": "4",
      "source": "parallax.mp4",
      "frame": "mid",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/code_out_v03/parallax.mp4",
      "also": [
        {
          "row": "4",
          "source": "triple.mp4",
          "at": "0:20"
        },
        {
          "row": "4",
          "source": "journey.mp4",
          "at": "0:28"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "n": 7,
      "at": "0:33",
      "start": 33.54,
      "end": 37.4,
      "text": "The nearest star to the Sun is called Proxima Centauri.",
      "row": "5",
      "source": "potw1343a.jpg",
      "frame": "still",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/proxima/potw1343a.jpg",
      "also": []
    },
    {
      "n": 8,
      "at": "0:38",
      "start": 38.16,
      "end": 43.88,
      "text": "It is a red dwarf, a small, cool star, far smaller and dimmer than ours.",
      "row": "5",
      "source": "eso1302a.jpg",
      "frame": "still",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/eso1302a.jpg",
      "also": [
        {
          "row": "5",
          "source": "eso1323a.jpg",
          "at": "0:41"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "n": 9,
      "at": "0:44",
      "start": 44.58,
      "end": 49.24,
      "text": "That is why you will never spot it by eye, even on the darkest night.",
      "row": "5",
      "source": "heic0809a.jpg",
      "frame": "still",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/heic0809a.jpg",
      "also": [
        {
          "row": "5",
          "source": "eso1323a.jpg",
          "at": "0:41"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "n": 10,
      "at": "0:50",
      "start": 50.14,
      "end": 53.08,
      "text": "It gives out less than one percent of the Sun's light.",
      "row": "6",
      "source": "GSFC_20171208_Archive_e002035.jpg",
      "frame": "still",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/sun/GSFC_20171208_Archive_e002035.jpg",
      "also": []
    },
    {
      "n": 11,
      "at": "0:53",
      "start": 53.78,
      "end": 56.28,
      "text": "But small stars burn their fuel slowly.",
      "row": "6",
      "source": "GSFC_20171208_Archive_e000790.jpg",
      "frame": "still",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/sun/GSFC_20171208_Archive_e000790.jpg",
      "also": [
        {
          "row": "6",
          "source": "GSFC_20171208_Archive_e002035.jpg",
          "at": "0:49"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "n": 12,
      "at": "0:56",
      "start": 56.98,
      "end": 63.2,
      "text": "Proxima will still be glowing for trillions of years, long after our own sun has gone.",
      "row": "6",
      "source": "eso1629i.jpg",
      "frame": "still",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/alphacen/eso1629i.jpg",
      "also": [
        {
          "row": "6",
          "source": "GSFC_20171208_Archive_e000790.jpg",
          "at": "0:54"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "n": 13,
      "at": "1:04",
      "start": 64.3,
      "end": 65.68,
      "text": "But it is not alone.",
      "row": "7",
      "source": "eso1629i.jpg",
      "frame": "still",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/alphacen/eso1629i.jpg",
      "also": []
    },
    {
      "n": 14,
      "at": "1:06",
      "start": 66.58,
      "end": 78.62,
      "text": "Close beside it in the sky are two much brighter stars, Alpha Centauri A and B, a pair a little further off at about four point three seven light-years.",
      "row": "7",
      "source": "bt_lasilla_crux.mp4",
      "frame": "in-point",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/timelapse/bt_lasilla_crux.mp4",
      "also": [
        {
          "row": "7",
          "source": "eso1629i.jpg",
          "at": "1:03"
        },
        {
          "row": "7",
          "source": "GSFC_20171208_Archive_e000214.jpg",
          "at": "1:13"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "n": 15,
      "at": "1:19",
      "start": 79.68,
      "end": 84.94,
      "text": "From the Southern Hemisphere, they shine as one of the brightest points in the whole night sky.",
      "row": "7",
      "source": "eso1241a.mp4",
      "frame": "in-point",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/timelapse/eso1241a.mp4",
      "also": [
        {
          "row": "7",
          "source": "eso0905a.jpg",
          "at": "1:22"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "n": 16,
      "at": "1:25",
      "start": 85.56,
      "end": 87.8,
      "text": "From Britain, they never rise.",
      "row": "7",
      "source": "eso0905a.jpg",
      "frame": "still",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/eso0905a.jpg",
      "also": []
    },
    {
      "n": 17,
      "at": "1:28",
      "start": 88.88,
      "end": 90.54,
      "text": "The three are one family.",
      "row": "8",
      "source": "triple.mp4",
      "frame": "mid",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/code_out_v01/triple.mp4",
      "also": []
    },
    {
      "n": 18,
      "at": "1:31",
      "start": 91.14,
      "end": 98.72,
      "text": "Proxima loops around the bright pair at a vast distance, and one orbit takes it about half a million years.",
      "row": "8",
      "source": "eso0844a.jpg",
      "frame": "still",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/eso0844a.jpg",
      "also": [
        {
          "row": "8",
          "source": "triple.mp4",
          "at": "1:28"
        },
        {
          "row": "8",
          "source": "uhd_bt_paranal_07.mp4",
          "at": "1:38"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "n": 19,
      "at": "1:39",
      "start": 99.78,
      "end": 107.74,
      "text": "When anyone says the nearest star, they mean the faint one, Proxima, four point two four light-years away.",
      "row": "8",
      "source": "uhd_bt_paranal_07.mp4",
      "frame": "in-point",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/timelapse/uhd_bt_paranal_07.mp4",
      "also": [
        {
          "row": "8",
          "source": "eso1250a_8k.jpg",
          "at": "1:43"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "n": 20,
      "at": "1:48",
      "start": 108.9,
      "end": 111.88,
      "text": "A light-year is a distance, not a time.",
      "row": "9",
      "source": "journey.mp4",
      "frame": "mid",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/code_out_v01/journey.mp4",
      "also": []
    },
    {
      "n": 21,
      "at": "1:52",
      "start": 112.5,
      "end": 115.08,
      "text": "It is how far light travels in a year.",
      "row": "9",
      "source": "iss073e0982679.jpg",
      "frame": "still",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/nightsky/iss073e0982679.jpg",
      "also": []
    },
    {
      "n": 22,
      "at": "1:55",
      "start": 115.88,
      "end": 121.32,
      "text": "So when you look towards Proxima, you are seeing light that left it more than four years ago.",
      "row": "9",
      "source": "eso1031a.jpg",
      "frame": "still",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/eso1031a.jpg",
      "also": [
        {
          "row": "9",
          "source": "iss073e0982679.jpg",
          "at": "1:52"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "n": 23,
      "at": "2:02",
      "start": 122.14,
      "end": 125.3,
      "text": "How do you measure the distance to something you can never visit?",
      "row": "10",
      "source": "GSFC_20171208_Archive_e000256.jpg",
      "frame": "still",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/nightsky/GSFC_20171208_Archive_e000256.jpg",
      "also": [
        {
          "row": "10",
          "source": "iss073e0982261.jpg",
          "at": "2:04"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "n": 24,
      "at": "2:06",
      "start": 126.58,
      "end": 127.22,
      "text": "Try this.",
      "row": "10",
      "source": "iss073e0982261.jpg",
      "frame": "still",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/nightsky/iss073e0982261.jpg",
      "also": []
    },
    {
      "n": 25,
      "at": "2:08",
      "start": 128.1,
      "end": 130.34,
      "text": "Hold up your thumb at arm's length.",
      "row": "11",
      "source": "uhd_yb_paranal_02.mp4",
      "frame": "in-point",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/timelapse/uhd_yb_paranal_02.mp4",
      "also": []
    },
    {
      "n": 26,
      "at": "2:11",
      "start": 131.26,
      "end": 133.4,
      "text": "Close one eye, then the other.",
      "row": "11",
      "source": "uhd_yb_paranal_02.mp4",
      "frame": "in-point",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/timelapse/uhd_yb_paranal_02.mp4",
      "also": [
        {
          "row": "11",
          "source": "iss073e0982679.jpg",
          "at": "2:12"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "n": 27,
      "at": "2:14",
      "start": 134.52,
      "end": 136.76,
      "text": "Your thumb jumps against the background.",
      "row": "11",
      "source": "iss073e0982679.jpg",
      "frame": "still",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/nightsky/iss073e0982679.jpg",
      "also": []
    },
    {
      "n": 28,
      "at": "2:17",
      "start": 137.48,
      "end": 140.2,
      "text": "The closer your thumb, the bigger the jump.",
      "row": "11",
      "source": "eso1323a.jpg",
      "frame": "still",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/eso1323a.jpg",
      "also": [
        {
          "row": "11",
          "source": "iss073e0982679.jpg",
          "at": "2:12"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "n": 29,
      "at": "2:21",
      "start": 141.4,
      "end": 143.36,
      "text": "Your two eyes are a ruler.",
      "row": "11",
      "source": "eso1323a.jpg",
      "frame": "still",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/eso1323a.jpg",
      "also": []
    },
    {
      "n": 30,
      "at": "2:24",
      "start": 144.36,
      "end": 148.22,
      "text": "Astronomers use the same trick with the whole of Earth's orbit.",
      "row": "12",
      "source": "parallax.mp4",
      "frame": "mid",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/code_out_v03/parallax.mp4",
      "also": []
    },
    {
      "n": 31,
      "at": "2:29",
      "start": 149.1,
      "end": 154.36,
      "text": "Photograph a star in January and again in July from the other side of the Sun.",
      "row": "12",
      "source": "eso0934a.jpg",
      "frame": "still",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/nightsky/eso0934a.jpg",
      "also": [
        {
          "row": "12",
          "source": "vltfromvistatimelapse.mp4",
          "at": "2:32"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "n": 32,
      "at": "2:35",
      "start": 155.5,
      "end": 161.68,
      "text": "A nearby star shifts a tiny amount against the far more distant stars behind it.",
      "row": "12",
      "source": "GSFC_20171208_Archive_e000256.jpg",
      "frame": "still",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/nightsky/GSFC_20171208_Archive_e000256.jpg",
      "also": [
        {
          "row": "12",
          "source": "vltfromvistatimelapse.mp4",
          "at": "2:32"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "n": 33,
      "at": "2:42",
      "start": 162.7,
      "end": 166.12,
      "text": "Measure the shift, and geometry gives you the distance.",
      "row": "12",
      "source": "GSFC_20171208_Archive_e000214.jpg",
      "frame": "still",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/proxima/GSFC_20171208_Archive_e000214.jpg",
      "also": []
    },
    {
      "n": 34,
      "at": "2:47",
      "start": 167.18,
      "end": 169.58,
      "text": "The shift is unbelievably small.",
      "row": "13",
      "source": "Tycho_Brahe.jpg",
      "frame": "still",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/portraits/Tycho_Brahe.jpg",
      "also": []
    },
    {
      "n": 35,
      "at": "2:50",
      "start": 170.3,
      "end": 177.66,
      "text": "For centuries, nobody could see it at all, and some astronomers took that as proof that Earth must stand still.",
      "row": "13",
      "source": "eso0932a.jpg",
      "frame": "still",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/nightsky/eso0932a.jpg",
      "also": [
        {
          "row": "13",
          "source": "Tycho_Brahe.jpg",
          "at": "2:46"
        },
        {
          "row": "13",
          "source": "eso1031a.jpg",
          "at": "2:56"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "n": 36,
      "at": "2:58",
      "start": 178.88,
      "end": 181.08,
      "text": "The real reason was the distance.",
      "row": "13",
      "source": "eso1031a.jpg",
      "frame": "still",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/eso1031a.jpg",
      "also": []
    },
    {
      "n": 37,
      "at": "3:02",
      "start": 182.32,
      "end": 189.72,
      "text": "In eighteen thirty-eight, the astronomer Friedrich Bessel measured it for a star called 61 Cygni.",
      "row": "14",
      "source": "parallax.mp4",
      "frame": "mid",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/code_out_v03/parallax.mp4",
      "also": [
        {
          "row": "14",
          "source": "eso0934a.jpg",
          "at": "3:06"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "n": 38,
      "at": "3:10",
      "start": 190.68,
      "end": 196.34,
      "text": "The angle he found was like the width of a coin seen from about thirteen kilometers away.",
      "row": "14",
      "source": "Bessel_Herterich_1825.jpg",
      "frame": "still",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/portraits/Bessel_Herterich_1825.jpg",
      "also": [
        {
          "row": "14",
          "source": "eso0934a.jpg",
          "at": "3:06"
        },
        {
          "row": "14",
          "source": "eso1250a_8k.jpg",
          "at": "3:15"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "n": 39,
      "at": "3:17",
      "start": 197.44,
      "end": 204.46,
      "text": "It was the first time anyone had measured the distance to a star, and it showed how deep the sky really is.",
      "row": "14",
      "source": "uhd_bt_paranal_01.mp4",
      "frame": "in-point",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/timelapse/uhd_bt_paranal_01.mp4",
      "also": [
        {
          "row": "14",
          "source": "eso1250a_8k.jpg",
          "at": "3:15"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "n": 40,
      "at": "3:25",
      "start": 205.78,
      "end": 213.02,
      "text": "Today, a European spacecraft called Gaia has measured these shifts for more than a billion stars.",
      "row": "15",
      "source": "gaia_sky_in_colour.jpg",
      "frame": "still",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/gaia/gaia_sky_in_colour.jpg",
      "also": [
        {
          "row": "15",
          "source": "eso0844a.jpg",
          "at": "3:29"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "n": 41,
      "at": "3:34",
      "start": 214.1,
      "end": 218.08,
      "text": "Proxima's is the largest of all because it is the nearest.",
      "row": "15",
      "source": "gaia_sky_in_colour.jpg",
      "frame": "still",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/gaia/gaia_sky_in_colour.jpg",
      "also": [
        {
          "row": "15",
          "source": "eso0844a.jpg",
          "at": "3:29"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "n": 42,
      "at": "3:39",
      "start": 219.1,
      "end": 223.84,
      "text": "Even so, it is like seeing a coin from about five kilometers away.",
      "row": "15",
      "source": "GSFC_20171208_Archive_e001982.jpg",
      "frame": "still",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/earth_moon/GSFC_20171208_Archive_e001982.jpg",
      "also": [
        {
          "row": "15",
          "source": "gaia_sky_in_colour.jpg",
          "at": "3:34"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "n": 43,
      "at": "3:44",
      "start": 224.94,
      "end": 226.96,
      "text": "We make one of these every week.",
      "row": "16",
      "source": "starfield.mp4",
      "frame": "mid",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/024_What-Happens-If-You-Travel-Near-Light-Speed/07_Edit-Project/graphics_v03/starfield.mp4",
      "also": []
    },
    {
      "n": 44,
      "at": "3:47",
      "start": 227.98,
      "end": 231.08,
      "text": "Subscribing is how the next one finds you.",
      "row": "16",
      "source": "heic1007a.jpg",
      "frame": "still",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/heic1007a.jpg",
      "also": []
    },
    {
      "n": 45,
      "at": "3:52",
      "start": 232.96,
      "end": 239.06,
      "text": "Numbers like four light-years are hard to feel, so let's shrink everything down.",
      "row": "17",
      "source": "eso1302a.jpg",
      "frame": "still",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/eso1302a.jpg",
      "also": [
        {
          "row": "17",
          "source": "starfield.mp4",
          "at": "3:52"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "n": 46,
      "at": "3:59",
      "start": 239.9,
      "end": 243.08,
      "text": "Make the Sun the size of a grapefruit and put it on a table.",
      "row": "18",
      "source": "scale.mp4",
      "frame": "mid",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/code_out_v01/scale.mp4",
      "also": []
    },
    {
      "n": 47,
      "at": "4:03",
      "start": 243.96,
      "end": 249.56,
      "text": "At that scale, Earth is a pinhead about fifteen meters away across a big room.",
      "row": "18",
      "source": "heic1007a.jpg",
      "frame": "still",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/heic1007a.jpg",
      "also": [
        {
          "row": "18",
          "source": "scale.mp4",
          "at": "4:03"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "n": 48,
      "at": "4:10",
      "start": 250.48,
      "end": 255.98,
      "text": "Everything you have ever known, every person, every city sits on that pin.",
      "row": "19",
      "source": "GSFC_20171208_Archive_e002130.jpg",
      "frame": "still",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/earth_moon/GSFC_20171208_Archive_e002130.jpg",
      "also": [
        {
          "row": "19",
          "source": "GSFC_20171208_Archive_e000868.jpg",
          "at": "4:14"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "n": 49,
      "at": "4:16",
      "start": 256.84,
      "end": 262.78,
      "text": "The farthest any human has ever traveled to the Moon is only about four centimeters from it.",
      "row": "19",
      "source": "GSFC_20171208_Archive_e001788.jpg",
      "frame": "still",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/earth_moon/GSFC_20171208_Archive_e001788.jpg",
      "also": [
        {
          "row": "19",
          "source": "GSFC_20171208_Archive_e000868.jpg",
          "at": "4:14"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "n": 50,
      "at": "4:23",
      "start": 263.86,
      "end": 265.48,
      "text": "Now, where is the nearest star?",
      "row": "20",
      "source": "GSFC_20171208_Archive_e002130.jpg",
      "frame": "still",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/earth_moon/GSFC_20171208_Archive_e002130.jpg",
      "also": []
    },
    {
      "n": 51,
      "at": "4:26",
      "start": 266.38,
      "end": 271.58,
      "text": "Proxima becomes a cherry, and that cherry is about four thousand kilometers away.",
      "row": "20",
      "source": "GSFC_20171208_Archive_e001788.jpg",
      "frame": "still",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/earth_moon/GSFC_20171208_Archive_e001788.jpg",
      "also": [
        {
          "row": "20",
          "source": "GSFC_20171208_Archive_e002130.jpg",
          "at": "4:23"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "n": 52,
      "at": "4:32",
      "start": 272.56,
      "end": 276.92,
      "text": "Put the grapefruit in London, and the cherry is further away than Cairo.",
      "row": "20",
      "source": "iss025e015176.jpg",
      "frame": "still",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/earth_moon/iss025e015176.jpg",
      "also": []
    },
    {
      "n": 53,
      "at": "4:37",
      "start": 277.8,
      "end": 287.18,
      "text": "A little beyond it sit the bright pair, Alpha Centauri A and B, one about the size of a big grapefruit, the other more like an orange.",
      "row": "21",
      "source": "starfield.mp4",
      "frame": "mid",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/024_What-Happens-If-You-Travel-Near-Light-Speed/07_Edit-Project/graphics_v03/starfield.mp4",
      "also": [
        {
          "row": "21",
          "source": "bt_lasilla_crux.mp4",
          "at": "4:37"
        },
        {
          "row": "21",
          "source": "eso0905a.jpg",
          "at": "4:46"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "n": 54,
      "at": "4:47",
      "start": 287.88,
      "end": 289.54,
      "text": "Between them, almost nothing.",
      "row": "21",
      "source": "eso0905a.jpg",
      "frame": "still",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/eso0905a.jpg",
      "also": []
    },
    {
      "n": 55,
      "at": "4:50",
      "start": 290.2,
      "end": 295.4,
      "text": "A few specks of dust and an emptiness so complete that it is hard to picture.",
      "row": "21",
      "source": "heic0809a.jpg",
      "frame": "still",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/heic0809a.jpg",
      "also": [
        {
          "row": "21",
          "source": "eso0905a.jpg",
          "at": "4:46"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "n": 56,
      "at": "4:56",
      "start": 296.4,
      "end": 298.06,
      "text": "And our farthest spacecraft?",
      "row": "22",
      "source": "PIA17049.jpg",
      "frame": "still",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/voyager/PIA17049.jpg",
      "also": []
    },
    {
      "n": 57,
      "at": "4:58",
      "start": 298.9,
      "end": 301.7,
      "text": "Voyager One, launched in nineteen seventy-seven.",
      "row": "22",
      "source": "PIA17049.jpg",
      "frame": "still",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/voyager/PIA17049.jpg",
      "also": [
        {
          "row": "22",
          "source": "PIA21739.jpg",
          "at": "5:00"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "n": 58,
      "at": "5:02",
      "start": 302.36,
      "end": 309.2,
      "text": "After nearly fifty years of flying, at this scale, it has traveled about two and a half kilometers from the grapefruit.",
      "row": "22",
      "source": "PIA21739.jpg",
      "frame": "still",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/voyager/PIA21739.jpg",
      "also": [
        {
          "row": "22",
          "source": "PIA21746.jpg",
          "at": "5:06"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "n": 59,
      "at": "5:09",
      "start": 309.8,
      "end": 311.36,
      "text": "It has barely left the town.",
      "row": "22",
      "source": "PIA21746.jpg",
      "frame": "still",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/voyager/PIA21746.jpg",
      "also": []
    },
    {
      "n": 60,
      "at": "5:12",
      "start": 312.28,
      "end": 314.4,
      "text": "So how long would the journey take?",
      "row": "23",
      "source": "PIA17464.jpg",
      "frame": "still",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/voyager/PIA17464.jpg",
      "also": []
    },
    {
      "n": 61,
      "at": "5:15",
      "start": 315.26,
      "end": 323.26,
      "text": "Walk at a steady pace, never stopping, never sleeping, and you would reach Proxima in about nine hundred million years.",
      "row": "24",
      "source": "journey.mp4",
      "frame": "mid",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/code_out_v01/journey.mp4",
      "also": [
        {
          "row": "24",
          "source": "PIA04495.jpg",
          "at": "5:20"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "n": 62,
      "at": "5:24",
      "start": 324.02,
      "end": 331.62,
      "text": "Take a car at motorway speed, and it is about forty-six million years, far longer than humans have existed.",
      "row": "24",
      "source": "PIA21747.jpg",
      "frame": "still",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/voyager/PIA21747.jpg",
      "also": [
        {
          "row": "24",
          "source": "PIA04495.jpg",
          "at": "5:20"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "n": 63,
      "at": "5:32",
      "start": 332.6,
      "end": 336.16,
      "text": "A jet airliner cuts it to about five million years.",
      "row": "24",
      "source": "PIA21739.jpg",
      "frame": "still",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/voyager/PIA21739.jpg",
      "also": []
    },
    {
      "n": 64,
      "at": "5:36",
      "start": 336.98,
      "end": 345.62,
      "text": "Voyager One is the fastest thing we have ever sent out of the Solar System, moving at about seventeen kilometers every second.",
      "row": "25",
      "source": "PIA14111.jpg",
      "frame": "still",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/voyager/PIA14111.jpg",
      "also": [
        {
          "row": "25",
          "source": "PIA21746.jpg",
          "at": "5:41"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "n": 65,
      "at": "5:46",
      "start": 346.16,
      "end": 354.26,
      "text": "It is not heading towards Proxima, but at its speed, crossing the same distance would take about seventy-five thousand years.",
      "row": "25",
      "source": "PIA17464.jpg",
      "frame": "still",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/voyager/PIA17464.jpg",
      "also": [
        {
          "row": "25",
          "source": "uhd_bt_paranal_07.mp4",
          "at": "5:45"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "n": 66,
      "at": "5:55",
      "start": 355.22,
      "end": 361.44,
      "text": "Even light at three hundred thousand kilometers a second needs four years and three months.",
      "row": "26",
      "source": "PIA21839.jpg",
      "frame": "still",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/voyager/PIA21839.jpg",
      "also": []
    },
    {
      "n": 67,
      "at": "6:02",
      "start": 362.16,
      "end": 364.12,
      "text": "Put that beside the light you know.",
      "row": "27",
      "source": "lighttimes.mp4",
      "frame": "mid",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/code_out_v03/lighttimes.mp4",
      "also": []
    },
    {
      "n": 68,
      "at": "6:04",
      "start": 364.92,
      "end": 367.58,
      "text": "Moonlight reaches you in just over a second.",
      "row": "27",
      "source": "lighttimes.mp4",
      "frame": "mid",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/code_out_v03/lighttimes.mp4",
      "also": []
    },
    {
      "n": 69,
      "at": "6:08",
      "start": 368.18,
      "end": 370.4,
      "text": "Sunlight takes about eight minutes.",
      "row": "27",
      "source": "lighttimes.mp4",
      "frame": "mid",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/code_out_v03/lighttimes.mp4",
      "also": []
    },
    {
      "n": 70,
      "at": "6:11",
      "start": 371.04,
      "end": 378.1,
      "text": "Light from the nearest star takes more than four years, and that is the shortest trip of its kind there is.",
      "row": "27",
      "source": "lighttimes.mp4",
      "frame": "mid",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/code_out_v03/lighttimes.mp4",
      "also": []
    },
    {
      "n": 71,
      "at": "6:18",
      "start": 378.98,
      "end": 381.2,
      "text": "So what is waiting at the end of the journey?",
      "row": "28",
      "source": "eso1629a.jpg",
      "frame": "still",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/proxima_b/eso1629a.jpg",
      "also": []
    },
    {
      "n": 72,
      "at": "6:21",
      "start": 381.9,
      "end": 385.5,
      "text": "In 2016, astronomers found a planet around Proxima.",
      "row": "28",
      "source": "eso1629d_video.mp4",
      "frame": "in-point",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/proxima_b/eso1629d_video.mp4",
      "also": [
        {
          "row": "28",
          "source": "eso1629a.jpg",
          "at": "6:18"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "n": 73,
      "at": "6:26",
      "start": 386.38,
      "end": 395.96,
      "text": "Proxima b is at least about as massive as Earth, and it circles its star every 11 days, close enough to sit in the zone where water could be liquid.",
      "row": "28",
      "source": "eso1629a.jpg",
      "frame": "still",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/proxima_b/eso1629a.jpg",
      "also": [
        {
          "row": "28",
          "source": "eso1629d_video.mp4",
          "at": "6:23"
        },
        {
          "row": "28",
          "source": "eso1629e_video.mp4",
          "at": "6:31"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "n": 74,
      "at": "6:36",
      "start": 396.84,
      "end": 398.84,
      "text": "But do not picture a second Earth yet.",
      "row": "29",
      "source": "eso1629e.jpg",
      "frame": "still",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/proxima_b/eso1629e.jpg",
      "also": []
    },
    {
      "n": 75,
      "at": "6:39",
      "start": 399.4,
      "end": 403.18,
      "text": "Nobody knows what its surface is like or whether it has air at all.",
      "row": "29",
      "source": "eso1629e_video.mp4",
      "frame": "in-point",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/proxima_b/eso1629e_video.mp4",
      "also": [
        {
          "row": "29",
          "source": "eso1629e.jpg",
          "at": "6:36"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "n": 76,
      "at": "6:43",
      "start": 403.98,
      "end": 405.64,
      "text": "Its star is a violent one.",
      "row": "30",
      "source": "eso1629e.jpg",
      "frame": "still",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/proxima_b/eso1629e.jpg",
      "also": []
    },
    {
      "n": 77,
      "at": "6:46",
      "start": 406.08,
      "end": 413.98,
      "text": "Proxima throws out flares, sudden blasts of energy that, for a star its size, are far more violent than our sun's.",
      "row": "30",
      "source": "GSFC_20160426_SDO_m12224_SolarFlare.mp4",
      "frame": "in-point",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/sun/GSFC_20160426_SDO_m12224_SolarFlare.mp4",
      "also": [
        {
          "row": "30",
          "source": "eso1629e.jpg",
          "at": "6:43"
        },
        {
          "row": "30",
          "source": "GSFC_20160426_SDO_m12224_SolarFlare.mp4",
          "at": "6:52"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "n": 78,
      "at": "6:54",
      "start": 414.68,
      "end": 417.06,
      "text": "They may have stripped any atmosphere away.",
      "row": "30",
      "source": "GSFC_20160426_SDO_m12224_SolarFlare.mp4",
      "frame": "in-point",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/sun/GSFC_20160426_SDO_m12224_SolarFlare.mp4",
      "also": []
    },
    {
      "n": 79,
      "at": "6:58",
      "start": 418.12,
      "end": 421.2,
      "text": "Whether Proxima b could ever be friendly is still open.",
      "row": "30",
      "source": "GSFC_20171208_Archive_e000759.jpg",
      "frame": "still",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/sun/GSFC_20171208_Archive_e000759.jpg",
      "also": []
    },
    {
      "n": 80,
      "at": "7:01",
      "start": 421.9,
      "end": 423.1,
      "text": "Could we ever go and look?",
      "row": "31",
      "source": "ACD24-0020-061.jpg",
      "frame": "still",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/sail/ACD24-0020-061.jpg",
      "also": []
    },
    {
      "n": 81,
      "at": "7:04",
      "start": 424.04,
      "end": 436.2,
      "text": "One plan, called Breakthrough Starshot, imagines probes weighing about as much as a paperclip pushed by giant lasers to a fifth of the speed of light, arriving in about 20 years.",
      "row": "31",
      "source": "ACS3_SolarPanels_001.jpg",
      "frame": "still",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/sail/ACS3_SolarPanels_001.jpg",
      "also": [
        {
          "row": "31",
          "source": "ACD24-0020-061.jpg",
          "at": "7:01"
        },
        {
          "row": "31",
          "source": "CamA_Seq109_2024-08-28_17-17-11Z_V2_S560161.jpg",
          "at": "7:12"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "n": 82,
      "at": "7:16",
      "start": 436.9,
      "end": 438.62,
      "text": "Nothing like it has been built yet.",
      "row": "31",
      "source": "CamC_Seq109_2024-08-28_17-17-13Z_V2_S595171.jpg",
      "frame": "still",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/sail/CamC_Seq109_2024-08-28_17-17-13Z_V2_S595171.jpg",
      "also": []
    },
    {
      "n": 83,
      "at": "7:19",
      "start": 439.12,
      "end": 441.56,
      "text": "It is a plan, and a very hard one.",
      "row": "31",
      "source": "CamC_Seq109_2024-08-28_17-17-13Z_V2_S595171.jpg",
      "frame": "still",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/sail/CamC_Seq109_2024-08-28_17-17-13Z_V2_S595171.jpg",
      "also": []
    },
    {
      "n": 84,
      "at": "7:22",
      "start": 442.7,
      "end": 444.76,
      "text": "Even a simple hello is slow.",
      "row": "32",
      "source": "PIA23214.jpg",
      "frame": "still",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/dsn/PIA23214.jpg",
      "also": []
    },
    {
      "n": 85,
      "at": "7:25",
      "start": 445.5,
      "end": 450.4,
      "text": "A radio message sent from Earth tonight would arrive in early 2031.",
      "row": "32",
      "source": "PIA24163.jpg",
      "frame": "still",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/dsn/PIA24163.jpg",
      "also": [
        {
          "row": "32",
          "source": "PIA23214.jpg",
          "at": "7:22"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "n": 86,
      "at": "7:31",
      "start": 451.28,
      "end": 456.94,
      "text": "If someone there answered straight away, the earliest reply would reach us in 2035.",
      "row": "32",
      "source": "PIA25136.jpg",
      "frame": "still",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/dsn/PIA25136.jpg",
      "also": [
        {
          "row": "32",
          "source": "PIA24163.jpg",
          "at": "7:27"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "n": 87,
      "at": "7:37",
      "start": 457.86,
      "end": 467.98,
      "text": "So this is the nearest star, a faint red sun you cannot see more than four light-years away with a world we cannot yet know.",
      "row": "33",
      "source": "PIA26147.jpg",
      "frame": "still",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/dsn/PIA26147.jpg",
      "also": [
        {
          "row": "33",
          "source": "PIA25137.jpg",
          "at": "7:43"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "n": 88,
      "at": "7:49",
      "start": 469.32,
      "end": 475.68,
      "text": "What if the most important thing about the nearest star is not how close it is but how far?",
      "row": "33",
      "source": "eso0932a.jpg",
      "frame": "still",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/nightsky/eso0932a.jpg",
      "also": [
        {
          "row": "33",
          "source": "uhd_bt_paranal_06.mp4",
          "at": "7:53"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "n": 89,
      "at": "7:56",
      "start": 476.74,
      "end": 479.82,
      "text": "The bigger question sits above you every clear night.",
      "row": "33",
      "source": "uhd_bt_paranal_06.mp4",
      "frame": "in-point",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/timelapse/uhd_bt_paranal_06.mp4",
      "also": [
        {
          "row": "33",
          "source": "vltfromvistatimelapse.mp4",
          "at": "7:59"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "n": 90,
      "at": "8:00",
      "start": 480.58,
      "end": 490.96,
      "text": "Each of those points of light is at least that far away, most of them far, far further, and we have only just begun to measure the gap",
      "row": "33",
      "source": "uhd_yb_paranal_02.mp4",
      "frame": "in-point",
      "path": "/Users/benjaminoats/YouTube/orbit-with-ben/02_Video-Projects/026_How-Far-Is-The-Nearest-Star/07_Edit-Project/pool_v01/timelapse/uhd_yb_paranal_02.mp4",
      "also": [
        {
          "row": "33",
          "source": "vltfromvistatimelapse.mp4",
          "at": "7:59"
        },
        {
          "row": "33",
          "source": "uhd_yb_paranal_01.mp4",
          "at": "8:09"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
